From 0c05f5cf8e7980ad0d6e0c7ce7aa13d85273ba17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:55:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] fix(steam): watch the x86-64 client until its first
 frame and recover

On an ARMv8.0 CPU the Steam menus are drawn by an x86 steamwebhelper
under FEX through FEX's GL thunks. When its GPU process keeps failing,
Chromium gives up ("GPU process isn't usable") and the screen stays
empty for good: the session sat on "Waiting for Steam's first frame"
with nothing explaining why. droiddeck-steam-x64 already noticed this
but only logged it.

Until the app reports the session's first frame (it now writes
~/.bl-first-frame), a watch beside the client:
- restarts the client once with software rendering when the GPU
  renderer gives up, and remembers that for this client build (a new
  build tries the GPU again);
- restarts it the same way when it has done nothing for 3 minutes
  (after 5) on the GPU renderer, and only reports it in software mode;
- says every 30 s how long it has been starting, the client's CPU use,
  free memory, whether the bootstrapper is updating or verifying, and a
  missing library if a web helper could not load one.
The session restarts the client at most once for this. The loading
screen shows these steps in the app's language.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
